---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this site stores on your device and what it never sends anywhere."
>
  <div class="container prose-page">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>Short version: nothing you do here leaves your device.</p>

    <h2>What is stored, and where</h2>
    <p>
      A few things are kept in your browser's local storage so the site remembers you: your reading level,
      your theme (light or dark), which topics you have opened or marked complete, and your practice data
      (your answers, a mastery estimate per concept, the review schedule and the days you practised). They
      live only in this browser on this device. Clearing site data removes them; the progress menu has a
      "Reset progress" button, and the <a href="/progress/">progress page</a> can export, import or reset your
      practice data.
    </p>
    <p>
      If your browser blocks storage, the site still works. It simply forgets your choices when you close the
      page.
    </p>

    <h2>What is not done</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No analytics, no advertising and no tracking scripts.</li>
      <li>No accounts unless you switch on sync, and no cookies set by this site's own code.</li>
      <li>Files you open in the tools are read in your browser and never uploaded.</li>
      <li>Search runs on an index shipped with the site, in your browser.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Optional sync</h2>
    <p>
      Sync across devices is off unless you switch it on from the progress page with "Sign in to sync". Until
      you press that button, no Firebase code is even downloaded. If you sign in (with Google, through
      Firebase Authentication):
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        One record is stored in Google Cloud Firestore for your account: your practice data as described above
        and the time of the last update. Security rules let only you read or change it.
      </li>
      <li>Firebase Authentication keeps your Google account id and email so you can sign in.</li>
      <li>Reading progress, level and theme stay on your device and are not synced.</li>
      <li>
        "Delete my synced data" on the progress page removes the cloud record and signs you out. The copy in
        your browser stays until you reset it. The sign-in record itself can only be removed by the site owner
        in the Firebase console.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      On sites built without the Firebase settings, the sync button does not appear and nothing is ever sent.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The pages are served by Firebase Hosting. Like any web host it keeps ordinary server logs of requests,
      which are outside this site's control.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
